// `map`'s functoriality written over the list `map` of
// `../../model/data/recursive-lists.gandr`, a `def`: a rule names only the
// operations of its own block, so `map` and `compose` here are no operation
// the block declares and the rule is malformed. A law over a definition is
// admitted when the coincidence check runs over the definitions an
// import-connected component holds (#525); until then the law is stated over
// `map` presented as an operation, in `../../model/data/map-laws.gandr`.

/// Mapping twice fused into mapping once, over the `def`.
@[ refuses("MalformedForm") ]
theory MapLaws {
  sort L : Type;

  rule mapMap : map(f, map(g, xs)) <=> map(compose(f, g), xs);
}
